{% comment %}
  One product row in the header search panel.

  The theme's own cards were doing the work here — the vertical `product-card`
  above 768px and `product-card-horizontal` below — and neither reads well in a
  dropdown: the grid squeezed two horizontal cards into a phone-width panel, so
  a four-word product name wrapped to four lines and the price fell out of view.

  This is one row instead, at every width: a square packshot plate, an eyebrow,
  the name, the price. The panel grid decides how many rows sit side by side.

  The eyebrow is the product line. Names in this catalogue are written
  "line: flavour" (nanogreens+ probiotic: green apple), so the part before the
  colon is the line and the part after is what actually distinguishes one result
  from the next — splitting them puts the distinguishing half on its own line
  instead of at the end of a wrap. Names with no colon fall back to the product
  type, then the vendor, and print whole.

  Accepts:
  - product {Object} - the product to render.

  Usage:
  {% render 'CWC_search-result__product', product: product %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign card_title = product.title
  assign card_eyebrow = ''

  if product.title contains ':'
    assign title_parts = product.title | split: ':'
    assign card_eyebrow = title_parts[0] | strip

    comment
      Joined back rather than taking [1], so a name carrying a second colon
      keeps its tail instead of losing it.
    endcomment
    assign title_rest = title_parts | slice: 1, 9
    assign card_title = title_rest | join: ':' | strip
  elsif product.type != blank
    assign card_eyebrow = product.type
  else
    assign card_eyebrow = product.vendor
  endif

  assign card_alt = product.featured_media.alt | default: product.title

  assign on_sale = false
  if product.compare_at_price_min > product.price_min
    assign on_sale = true
  endif
-%}

<a href="{{ product.url }}" class="cwc_search-card" data-instant>
  <span class="cwc_search-card__media">
    {%- if product.featured_media != blank -%}
      {{-
        product.featured_media
        | image_url: width: 200
        | image_tag:
          loading: 'lazy',
          sizes: '80px',
          widths: '80,120,160,200',
          class: 'cwc_search-card__image',
          alt: card_alt
      -}}
    {%- endif -%}
  </span>

  <span class="cwc_search-card__body">
    {%- if card_eyebrow != blank -%}
      <span class="cwc_search-card__eyebrow">{{ card_eyebrow }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}

    <span class="cwc_search-card__title">{{ card_title }}</span>

    <span class="cwc_search-card__price">
      {%- comment -%}
        Struck price first, matching the way a price drop is read: what it was,
        then what it is.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if on_sale -%}
        <s class="cwc_search-card__was">{{ product.compare_at_price_min | money }}</s>
      {%- endif -%}

      <span class="cwc_search-card__now{% if on_sale %} cwc_search-card__now--sale{% endif %}">
        {%- if product.price_varies -%}
          {%- assign price_min = product.price_min | money -%}
          {{- 'product.price.from_price_html' | t: price_min: price_min -}}
        {%- else -%}
          {{- product.price | money -}}
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>

      {%- unless product.available -%}
        <span class="cwc_search-card__flag">{{ 'product.general.sold_out_button' | t }}</span>
      {%- endunless -%}
    </span>
  </span>
</a>
